# A corrupted save's memory card prompt: "Erase this and create new Game
# Data?" with No hovered, the game's default, said with the keys. Left says
# "Yes", and A on it erases the save and creates a new one: "Erasing the
# corrupted data..." and "Creating new Game Data." each show for one frame
# only and are never said, and the result is said with its key. A again
# goes on to the opening movie.
# The save is a fresh one (memcard_create.drive's), corrupted as it is
# copied in (drive.py --corrupt), never committed:
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/memcard_create.drive --card --out build/drive/fresh.log
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/memcard_corrupted.drive --corrupt \
#     "--card=build/drive/fresh.log.settings/USA/Card A/01-GALE-SuperSmashBros0110290334.gci"

wait 'speak queue \(off\): "The Game Data on the Memory Card in Slot A is corrupted\. Erase this and create new Game Data\? No\. Left and Right choose, A confirms\."$'
press Left
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "Yes"$'
press A
wait 'speak interrupt \(off\): "Game Data has been created\. This game saves data automatically while you play\. Please do not touch the Memory Card or POWER Button while saving or copying\. A to continue\."$'
press A
wait '"Opening movie\. Press Start to skip\."$'
